Linux 7.3 cfg80211 cookies: cfg80211 assigns the cookie, the driver reports it.

remain_on_channel, mgmt_tx and probe_client (now probe_peer) take the cookie by
value instead of returning one, and cfg80211_probe_status() gained a link_id.
The driver used to mint its own (a RoC counter, the skb pointer, a probe
counter); report the one cfg80211 handed in instead, or userspace cannot match
the events (wpa_supplicant drops mgmt TX status with an unknown cookie, which
SAE external auth relies on). Frames the driver sends on its own report 0.

Every change is gated on LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7, 3, 0).

